  "description": "<p>As noted in \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-790\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-790\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"FeSL AuthN fedora-users.xml not closed properly after each use\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-790\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n, FeSL's fedora-users.xml authentication implementation reads this file for every request to the repository.  This file should not have to be re-read and parsed for every request &#8211; the info it contains should be cached in some way for performance.  For example, a reasonable out-of-box behavior would be to refresh from the file if it has been &gt; 60 seconds since the last request.</p>",
